  "overview": {
    "text": "A sword is a hand-held weapon built around a long blade joined to a hilt; its grip and guard help the user hold and control it. Swords are not one fixed design: blade shape and edge distinguish forms intended chiefly for cutting, thrusting, or both, including curved sabres and straight double-edged blades. Their designs changed with fighting needs; for example, one fifteenth-century European sword at the Met has a pointed, double-edged blade suited to thrusting and slashing against armor. Historically swords served as weapons, but some also carried social meaning: decorated and ceremonial forms show their place in status and dress as well as combat.",
    "source_urls": [
      "https://oaktrust.library.tamu.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/4e77f086-d65f-47b0-9c4c-09dc09ade1ac/content",
      "https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/35388",
      "https://fitzmuseum.cam.ac.uk/about-us/collections/arms-and-armour"
    ]
  },
  "key_facts": [
    {
      "text": "A typical sword has a blade and a hilt; the hilt commonly includes a grip, guard, and pommel.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://oaktrust.library.tamu.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/4e77f086-d65f-47b0-9c4c-09dc09ade1ac/content"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Blade shape and construction vary with intended use: examples include cutting blades, narrow thrusting blades, and curved blades designed for cutting.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://oaktrust.library.tamu.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/4e77f086-d65f-47b0-9c4c-09dc09ade1ac/content"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Met’s two-handed sword, dated about 1400–1450, has a long, pointed, double-edged blade designed for thrusting and slashing; the museum says it could be used against plate armor.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/35388"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Met’s circa-1450 European sword has a simple cross-shaped hilt and a rounded blade tip; the museum identifies it as primarily a slashing weapon that could also thrust.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/27458"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sword types include broadswords, hand-and-a-half swords, sabres, rapiers, ceremonial swords, and specialized forms from Asia and the Islamic world.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://fitzmuseum.cam.ac.uk/about-us/collections/arms-and-armour"
      ]
    }
  ],
